# Build context for every image in infra/docker. Each Dockerfile installs dependencies
# and builds inside the image, so nothing produced on the host belongs in the context:
#
# - node_modules holds host-native binaries (Prisma engines, sharp) for the wrong OS, and
#   pnpm's links in it make BuildKit refuse the whole context on Windows.
# - build output would shadow what the image compiles for itself.
# - .env holds production secrets, and anything sent as context can end up in a layer or
#   in the build cache.
# - storage/ is uploaded media and backups: large, and customer data.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/storybook-static
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

storage
backups
e2e/test-results
e2e/playwright-report
.deploy-previous

npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
